<title>LITHUANIA: C.BANK RESERVES TOP ONE BILLION DOLLARS.</title>
<headline>C.BANK RESERVES TOP ONE BILLION DOLLARS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's central bank said on Thursday that its official reserves exceeded the one billion dollar mark for the first time.  </p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that its official reserves stood at $1.182 billion as of July 23, up from $939.6 million at the end of June.</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
